WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.020
- So it appears that the emoluments cases

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:03.410
against Former President Trump

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:05.930
have now all been dismissed as moot.

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.890
And while a lot of people are upset,

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:09.480
it's not as crazy as it seems

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.340
because federal courts have requirement

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.330
that all cases have to
be a case in controversy.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:15.980
So, the court can't decide things

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.330
where it doesn't have
any power to do anything.

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.410
And if you're thinking, "Well
he still made all that money

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:21.680
while he was president,"

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.800
you're right except that
a lot of these cases,

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.270
if not all of them, didn't
actually seek damages.

00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:27.850
They sought perspective relief.

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:30.190
They sought to stop him from
doing stuff in the future.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:32.520
They didn't actually
seek retrospective relief

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.590
to get him to disgorge
the benefits that he had.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:37.100
And since Trump is no longer president,

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.830
there's really nothing
that the courts can do now.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.600
That being said, it does
leave open the possibility

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.370
that someone, maybe the Biden DOJ,

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.310
might go after President Trump for damages

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.100
and force him to disgorge those benefits.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.960
Though there's always
the question of standing.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.153
So stay tuned, and I'll see you in court.

